Noteworthy runtime behaviors / risks identified (from logs + code)

Agent-state loop: Repetitive messages "Quantidade incorreta de agentes → reinicializando…" (log snapshot) indicate a bug where agent counts/state mismatch cause repeated reinitialization. Likely remediation: ensure consistent agent registry logic and idempotent initialization (look at agents.ts and agents endpoints).
React infinite loop: "Maximum update depth exceeded" → likely due to a hook/component that triggers state updates without stable dependencies (e.g., useEffect calling setState while depending on something that changes every render). Candidate areas: HybridAgentsStatsPanel.tsx, use-hybrid-agents.ts (the hook sets state for stats and refresh interval); ensure stable function refs (useCallback/useMemo) and avoid returning new arrays/objects on each render.
LLM rate failures: 500 + 429 observed for /api/llm-proxy calls — indicates provider errors or rate-limiter triggers. llm-proxy.ts has rate-limiting and retry with backoff, but 429/500 means either over rate-limit on provider or internal rate-limiter. Mitigation options: implement provider-specific rate limits, backoff and circuit breakers (already partly implemented), cache responses, or add usage quotas in the UI.
Hybrid agents disabled: hybrid-agents-integration.ts is a stub; logs warn "Hybrid Agents Integration está desabilitado (modo manutenção)". This indicates hybrid LangGraph workflow is intentionally disabled — plan to enable requires path alias/config fixes.
